Z||000011||btoth||04-03-2001||06:44 PM||||I am definatly planning on getting a remanufactured engine installed in my '86 GT.  I have done some searches of past threads, but what I want to know is if I get a 3.1 long block, what else besides the Fiero intakes and rocker arm covers needs to be transfered to the new engine?<P>I plan on having the work done by the local GM service dept.  I am not going to do this myself.  I just want to know what needs to be done so I can explain it to them if they doubt that it can be done.<P>(Or should I just stick with the 2.8?)||||reg||5
